./md-review-records/2026-08-13-sanity-checker-instructions/claude-restate-good.md:59:1. "Read the scorecard and the prompt draft's header, verify the four novel findings against current code, then offer the user the grid-seat walk — the decision this pile exists to reach." — Your opening sequence of work, in this order: first read `scorecard.md` from the attack-split experiment and the header block of `sanity-checker-prompt-draft.md` that records the settled operating rulings; second, check each of the four un-triaged novel findings against the code as it stands today to see whether each is still accurate; third, propose to the user that you conduct the item-by-item walk on whether the sanity-checker should take up seats in the md-review grid, that being the question this whole area of responsibility was created in order to settle. I read "offer" as meaning you propose the walk and let him accept, not that you begin walking unilaterally.
