./md-review-records/2026-08-13-seat-first-prompt/claude-hunt-good.md:53:Three cases. (a) "the recycle hook that hands off when context runs low" — the project has no such name; the mechanism is the `Stop` hook running `scripts/handoff-context-threshold-hook.py`, and grepping the repository for "recycle hook" finds nothing. (b) "the guard on instruction files" (line 7) and "a hook enforces this" (line 25) name the same thing two different ways within one document; the actual, greppable name is `instruction-file-guard.py`. (c) "the user's Mac-side review seat" — `CLAUDE.md` calls it "the user's Mac-side agent", `docs/agents/gatekeeper-instructions.md` and `sidebar-instructions.md` call it "the Mac-side seat", and `docs/issues/queue/45-ubuntu-fleet-open-work-inventory.md` calls it "the Mac-side review-and-merge seat". Harm: this is the one document a fresh seat is guaranteed to read, so its vocabulary propagates; an agent told to find "the recycle hook" or "the review seat" will search and find nothing, and cannot tell whether the thing is missing or merely named differently. This runs against `CLAUDE.md`'s naming rule, which requires checking invented names with grep and, on collision or ambiguity, using the existing name rather than a new one. Confidence: sure the names differ; unsure only whether any of them is intended as a deliberate umbrella term.
